      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking Sudafed while on lisinopril and with hypertension is generally unsafe because its active ingredient, pseudoephedrine, can raise blood pressure and increase heart rate. You should avoid using Sudafed and instead contact your doctor or pharmacist immediately for safe over-the-counter alternatives that won't interfere with your blood pressure medication. Please do not self-medicate with decongestants when you have a history of hypertension without professional approval first.",
